{
  "presses": ["L-index-top-in", "L-index-home-in", "R-index-top-in", "L-pinky-top"],
  "note": "Known: {A=L-index-top-in,B=L-index-home-in,C=R-index-top-in,D=R-index-home-in} held letters {D,H,P,Q} in some perm (T1). T2 chord={A,B,C,X=L-pinky-top}. Next: with observed sorted set S, if any letter not in {D,H,P,Q} => that letter = X; the other 3 letters give exact mapping for A,B,C. Then T3 use chord {A,B,D,Y} to resolve D similarly via elimination."
}

{
  "presses": ["L-pinky-top", "L-pinky-bottom", "L-ring-top", "R-index-bottom"],
  "locks": {
    "L-pinky-top": "Y"
  },
  "note": "Keep: L-pinky-top=Y (locked). T4 chord: L-pinky-top + {L-pinky-bottom, L-ring-top, R-index-bottom}. Next obs: set should include Y; remaining 3 letters map to those 3 keys (pre-rotation). Then use rotation notice to track any of these keys being shuffled."
}

{
  "presses": [
    "L-pinky-top",
    "L-index-top",
    "L-index-bottom-in",
    "L-ring-bottom"
  ],
  "note": "T4: L-pinky-top=Y (locked). Other pressed keys {L-pinky-bottom,L-ring-top,R-index-bottom} have letters {G,M,S} (perm unknown; none of them rotated). Rot post-T4 keys={L-index-bottom-in,L-index-top,L-ring-bottom} permuted among themselves (letters unknown). Plan T5 chord: {L-pinky-top,Y},{L-index-top},{L-index-bottom-in},{L-ring-bottom} to learn their current 3-letter set."
}

{
  "presses": ["L-ring-top", "L-ring-bottom", "L-middle-bottom", "L-ring-home"],
  "note": "Known now: L-pinky-top=Y, L-pinky-bottom=E, L-ring-top=M, L-ring-bottom=U, L-middle-bottom=S. Next (T12) press {L-ring-top,L-ring-bottom,L-middle-bottom,L-ring-home}; output sorted should be {M,U,S,?} so ? = (pre-rotation) letter on L-ring-home. If any of these 4 keys rotated on T12, mark L-ring-home uncertain."
}

{
  "presses": ["L-pinky-top", "L-ring-top", "R-index-home-in", "L-index-top-in"],
  "note": "T16 no-rot: {L-pinky-top,L-ring-top,R-index-home-in,L-middle-top} gave {Y,M,O,W}. So A=R-index-home-in ∈{O,W}; B=L-middle-top other. Plan T17 chord {Yanchor L-pinky-top, Manchor L-ring-top, A, C=L-index-top-in} => {Y,M,A,C}. T18 chord {Y,M,A,D=R-index-bottom-in} then intersect sets to get sym(A)."
}
